# Design System

Always use `@wordpress/components` for UI components. Avoid reimplementing patterns that already exist in the WordPress admin component library.

## Logical Properties

Use CSS logical properties instead of physical directional properties. This ensures correct layout in both LTR and RTL languages.

**Avoid:**

```typescript
<Box
  marginLeft={ theme.spacing(2) }
  paddingRight={ theme.spacing(1) }
  borderBottom="1px solid"
/>
```

**Prefer:**

```typescript
<Box
  marginInlineStart={ theme.spacing(2) }
  paddingInlineEnd={ theme.spacing(1) }
  borderBlockEnd="1px solid"
/>
```

Mapping reference:

| Physical                       | Logical                                   |
|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| `paddingLeft` / `paddingRight` | `paddingInlineStart` / `paddingInlineEnd` |
| `paddingTop` / `paddingBottom` | `paddingBlockStart` / `paddingBlockEnd`   |
| `marginLeft` / `marginRight`   | `marginInlineStart` / `marginInlineEnd`   |
| `marginTop` / `marginBottom`   | `marginBlockStart` / `marginBlockEnd`     |
| `borderLeft` / `borderRight`   | `borderInlineStart` / `borderInlineEnd`   |
| `borderTop` / `borderBottom`   | `borderBlockStart` / `borderBlockEnd`     |
| `left` / `right` (positioning) | `insetInlineStart` / `insetInlineEnd`     |
| `top` / `bottom` (positioning) | `insetBlockStart` / `insetBlockEnd`       |

Shorthand logical properties are preferred:

- `paddingBlock` / `paddingInline`
- `marginBlock` / `marginInline`
- `borderBlock` / `borderInline`
- `insetBlock` / `insetInline`
